# Deployment headers for Cloudflare Pages (also read by Netlify).
#
# Static files are copied to the output root verbatim, so this ships in the
# theme rather than per site: security is the default, not a reminder.
#
# Why the policy is strict
#   Every resource the theme ships is first-party, and every script and
#   stylesheet carries an SRI `integrity` attribute, so no directive needs
#   unsafe-inline, unsafe-eval or a third-party origin. js/carousel.js and
#   js/contact.js were moved out of their shortcodes specifically so this
#   could stay free of unsafe-inline; the JSON-LD blocks are exempt from
#   script-src (a non-executable script type) and are unaffected.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-src 'self' https://www.google.com https://maps.google.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Exceptions to this file, and why
#
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline'  The carousel writes a dynamic aspect-ratio
#     attribute (aspect-ratio: W / H) that has no class equivalent. Inline
#     style cannot execute code; removing this needs a nonce plan, and Hugo
#     does not generate nonces.
#
#   frame-src google origins   The map shortcode is the theme's explicit
#     opt-in to a third-party embed, documented with a Google Maps URL. Add
#     your provider's origin here rather than widening to https:
#
#   Ads  site.Params.ads.client turns on the AdSense loader, which this
#     policy blocks: pagead2.googlesyndication.com is a foreign origin in
#     script-src, and the ad frames, beacons and creatives are foreign
#     too. The push call is NOT the problem — the ads shortcode ships it
#     as an external js/ads.js with an integrity attribute, so no
#     directive needs unsafe-inline for it. An ad-enabled site must ship
#     its own static/_headers with the AdSense origins (the security docs
#     have a working block); the build fails until it does, because
#     Google changes ad origins over time and only a nonce-based policy
#     is officially supported — which a static host cannot generate.
#
#   frame-ancestors 'none'     Deletes if you want the site embeddable in an
#     iframe; the theme assumes it is not.
